cies like their secret powers  who were ruling  everything or that hiv was made up this  kind of stuff  since the pandemic you can assume that  there's an  increase but we don't know that yet for  sure  because we have no comparison before  and after the pandemic but if you look  at the social media channels you see  a huge increase on platforms like  telegram you see that they are  mobilizing more on the streets so  i don't know if there are more but yeah  it's more relevant for them right now  how dangerous is it to us as individuals  because we look at it from the outside  and say what are these people doing why  are they why do they believe that  how susceptible are we uh when it comes  to falling for conspiracy theories  when you look at disinformation wrong  claims we all believed in things that  are not true  that happens easily so i for myself  believed  for a long time that you eat eight  spiders in a lifetime  that's not true that's a fake news that  some journalists made up years ago when  the internet was  newer when it comes to conspiracies i  think also  many people actually believe  a little bit in them and what we do in  psychology is we measure the conspiracy  mentality that means the general  tendency to believe and conspiracy or  not and most people are on the scale in  the middle that means they believe a  little bit in it  and there are only a few who completely  refused it and don't have that mindset  and it's also the question if this is  better because people who have no  conspiracy mindset  i'd also say police they are doing  everything right  whatever they do i think they're amazing  and this is also not a critical  perspective on society so being in the  middle is actually not the worst thing  is this actually a a typical western  phenomenon  that we're talking about conspiracy  theories so conspiracy theories exist or  the belief in it access  all over the world psychologists um  yeah even think at least some of them  that it has an evolutionary basis so  that there is uh it's rooted in our  systems  um there's one bigger study that was  conducted in the summer and that looked  at  conspiracy beliefs in seven different  countries um  and for example in india 72 percent of  the  people believed that coronavirus is  actually a chinese bio weapon  that's a huge amount of people and  in the us for example it was 32 which is  still  every third person that believes that  kind of things  and when you look at narratives like  that 5g  this new phone network standard  is responsible for the corona virus in  germany you have seven percent who  believe that but in  jordan for example it's also one third  of the population and this is linked to  following the measures less like wearing  no face mask  or being not likely to get a vaccine  or also using violence so it is linked  to behavior  in the pandemic and it hinders us to  manage the pandemic  and i think it's important to have a  look at this on an early stage  and have concepts how to deal with that  because  these vaccine centers are likely to be  attacked  not maybe physically but that people go  there and  interrupt people in their work and yeah  we need concepts how to deal with that  and how to prepare the employees there  we've just entered the second year of  the pandemic will we see  even worse protests will conspiracy  theories thrive even more  i think it also depends on how um the  government reacts  so if a certain kind of protests are not  allowed  then they won't happen but they look of  course for other wastes like  giving flyers and stuff like that so  they try to react to the yeah  restrictions that they have but  of course the demonstration has another  powerful impact you see the pictures  they look  very motivating for the scene so it  depends on directions of the government  but i think especially the topic of  vaccination  was always since vaccinations were  invented part of conspiracy theories  and therefore that's crucial to reall